        "mission_intent": "We need a full Infrastructure Management process specification aligned with NIST SP 800-160 Volume 1 for our upcoming secure satellite ground station project (Project Meridian). The specification should define how infrastructure resources and services \u2014 including development environments, test labs, build servers, configuration management tooling, and communications networks \u2014 are identified, obtained, provisioned, and maintained to support both organizational and project-level security objectives across the entire system life cycle. It must address how infrastructure security requirements and security constraints are derived and flowed down so that all infrastructure resources, not just those directly providing a security function, are evaluated against applicable constraints. The spec should reference ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288:2015 Infrastructure Management process activities and outcomes as the process framework baseline, then overlay the security considerations from SP 800-160 Vol. 1 Chapter 3 regarding security functions, services, and constraint adequacy. Please include criteria for determining when an infrastructure resource is adequate to securely implement and support the project, roles and responsibilities for infrastructure provisioning decisions, traceability from infrastructure security constraints back to stakeholder protection needs, and a review cadence tied to major life-cycle stage gates. We need a draft ready for the systems engineering review board by end of next month.",
